 function `sklearn/datasets/_base.py:_fetch_remote`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1157 | def _fetch_remote(remote, dirname=None):\n1158 |     \"\"\"Helper function to download a remote dataset into path\n1159 | \n1160 |     Fetch a dataset pointed by remote's url, save into path using remote's\n1161 |     filename and ensure its integrity based on the SHA256 Checksum of the\n1162 |     downloaded file.\n1163 | \n1164 |     Parameters\n1165 |     ----------\n1166 |     remote : RemoteFileMetadata\n1167 |         Named tuple containing remote dataset meta information: url, filename\n1168 |         and checksum\n1169 | \n1170 |     dirname : string\n1171 |         Directory to save the file to.\n1172 | \n1173 |     Returns\n1174 |     -------\n1175 |     file_path: string\n1176 |         Full path of the created file.\n1177 |     \"\"\"\n1178 | \n1179 |     file_path = (remote.filename if dirname is None\n1180 |                  else join(dirname, remote.filename))\n1181 |     urlretrieve(remote.url, file_path)\n1182 |     checksum = _sha256(file_path)\n1183 |     if remote.checksum != checksum:\n1184 |         raise IOError(\"{} has an SHA256 checksum ({}) \"\n1185 |                       \"differing from expected ({}), \"\n1186 |                       \"file may be corrupted.\".format(file_path, checksum,\n1187 |                                                       remote.checksum))\n1188 |     return file_path\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"md5\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound code snippet in file `sklearn/datasets/_rcv1.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  1 | \"\"\"RCV1 dataset.\n  2 | \n  3 | The dataset page is available at\n  4 | \n  5 |     http://jmlr.csail.mit.edu/papers/volume5/lewis04a/\n  6 | \"\"\"\n  7 | \n  8 | # Author: Tom Dupre la Tour\n  9 | # License: BSD 3 clause\n 10 | \n 11 | import logging\n 12 | \n 13 | from os import remove, makedirs\n 14 | from os.path import dir