ef _get_submodule(module_name, submodule_name):\n22 |     \"\"\"Get the submodule docstring and automatically add the hook.\n23 | \n24 |     `module_name` is e.g. `sklearn.feature_extraction`, and `submodule_name` is e.g.\n25 |     `image`, so we get the docstring and hook for `sklearn.feature_extraction.image`\n26 |     submodule. `module_name` is used to reset the current module because autosummary\n27 |     automatically changes the current module.\n28 |     \"\"\"\n29 |     lines = [\n30 |         f\".. automodule:: {module_name}.{submodule_name}\",\n31 |         f\".. currentmodule:: {module_name}\",\n32 |     ]\n33 |     return \"\\n\\n\".join(lines)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"assert_consistent_docs docstring\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound `sklearn/utils/deprecation.py:deprecated`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  4 | import functools\n  5 | import warnings\n  6 | \n  7 | __all__ = [\"deprecated\"]\n  8 | \n  9 | \n 10 | class deprecated:\n 11 |     \"\"\"Decorator to mark a function or class as deprecated.\n 12 | \n 13 |     Issue a warning when the function is called/the class is instantiated and\n 14 |     adds a warning to the docstring.\n 15 | \n 16 |     The optional extra argument will be appended to the deprecation message\n 17 |     and the docstring. Note: to use this with the default value for extra, put\n 18 |     in an empty of parentheses:\n 19 | \n 20 |     Examples\n 21 |     --------\n 22 |     >>> from sklearn.utils import deprecated\n 23 |     >>> deprecated()\n 24 |     <sklearn.utils.deprecation.deprecated object at ...>\n 25 |     >>> @deprecated()\n 26 |     ... def some_function(): pass\n 27 | \n 28 |     Parameters\n 29 |     ----------\n 30 |     extra : str, default=''\n 31 |           To be added to the deprecation messages.\n 32 |     \"\"\"\n 33 | \n 34 |     # Adapted from https://wiki.python.org/moin/PythonDecoratorLibrary,\n 35 |     # but with many changes.\n 36 | \n 37 |     def __