mators that are given\n1488 |         estimator objects.\n1489 | \n1490 |     Returns\n1491 |     -------\n1492 |     decorated_fit : method\n1493 |         The decorated fit method.\n1494 |     \"\"\"\n1495 | \n1496 |     def decorator(fit_method):\n1497 |         @functools.wraps(fit_method)\n1498 |         def wrapper(estimator, *args, **kwargs):\n1499 |             global_skip_validation = get_config()[\"skip_parameter_validation\"]\n1500 | \n1501 |             # we don't want to validate again for each call to partial_fit\n1502 |             partial_fit_and_fitted = (\n1503 |                 fit_method.__name__ == \"partial_fit\" and _is_fitted(estimator)\n1504 |             )\n1505 | \n1506 |             if not global_skip_validation and not partial_fit_and_fitted:\n1507 |                 estimator._validate_params()\n1508 | \n1509 |             with config_context(\n1510 |                 skip_parameter_validation=(\n1511 |                     prefer_skip_nested_validation or global_skip_validation\n1512 |                 )\n1513 |             ):\n1514 |                 return fit_method(estimator, *args, **kwargs)\n1515 | \n1516 |         return wrapper\n1517 | \n1518 |     return decorator\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me explore the repository structure to understand where docstring-related functionality exists.\n\n<function=explore_tree_structure>\n<parameter=start_entities>['/']</parameter>\n<parameter=traversal_depth>2</parameter>\n<parameter=dependency_type_filter>['contains']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "explore_tree_structure", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 contains \u2500\u2500 .spin\n\u2502               \u2514\u2500\u2500 contains \u2500\u2500 .spin/cmds.py\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 contains \u2500\u2500 asv_benchmarks\n\u2502               \u2514\u2500\u2500 contains \u2500\u2500 asv_benchmarks/benchmarks\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 contains